  "name": "Medicine Ball Punch Throw",
  "definition": "A unilateral one-hand medicine-ball power throw from a fixed split boxing stance. The ball begins in the rear hand; the athlete pivots the rear foot, turns the hips and trunk, extends the rear arm, and releases the ball along a straight-punch direction, then retrieves or receives it and fully resets. The publisher source does not resolve the humeral path, so no shoulder motion is prime-authored. Two-hand chest passes, side throws, overhead throws, floor slams, locomotor approaches, retained implements, and reactive rebound catches remain outside this family.",
